<title>RUSSIA: Strike halts flights in Russian region - agency.</title>
<headline>Strike halts flights in Russian region - agency.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strike by air traffic controllers stopped flights to and from more than 30 airports in the oil-rich Tyumen region of western Siberia on Sunday, Russia's RIA news agency said.</p>
<p>The deputy chairman of the Russian air traffic controllers union, Gennady Borisov, told the agency the strikers were demanding higher pay and social welfare guarantees.</p>
<p>It was not clear how long the strike was planned to last.</p>
</text>
